Subject: [PATCH] net: proxy credentials from the launch payload

The profile switch can carry a two-key wrapper holding the device
profile and a proxy username and password. The browser answers SOCKS5,
SOCKS4 and HTTP proxy authentication with those credentials, up to three
rounds per connection, without prompting the user. HTTP proxy
credentials go into the auth cache, so later connections authenticate
without a 407 round trip. The credentials stay out of the profile
schema, diagnostics and anything written to disk.

